{
  "name": "PHASE 2C - REVISION REPLY CAPTURE",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 📥 PHASE 2C: REVISION REPLY CAPTURE (State Machine)\n\n### 📌 OVERVIEW\nA session-based, fault-tolerant natural language processor triggered by the **Master Router**. It intercepts plain-text messages from administrators, checks for active revision locks, translates messy human instructions into structured database commands, and executes parallel updates to both Supabase and Google Sheets.\n\n---\n\n### 🗺️ ARCHITECTURAL FLOW & BLOCKS\n\n#### 🔒 1. Session Validation Gate\n- Bypasses raw Telegram polling; receives merged payloads from the Master Router.\n- Queries `pending_revisions` in Supabase using the isolated `telegram_id`. \n- **Silent Exit:** If no session is found, the workflow gracefully terminates without acting on casual chat.\n\n#### ❌ 2. Ghost Session Mitigation (Cancel Path)\n- Evaluates the incoming text for the `/cancel` slash command.\n- If true, instantly flushes the `pending_revisions` lock and issues a clearance confirmation to the user, preventing downstream misroutes.\n\n#### 🤖 3. Fault-Tolerant AI Parsing\n- Replaces rigid Regex parameters with **Google Gemini (2.5 Flash)** to process natural human language (typos, shorthand, multi-day groupings).\n- Enforces a strict schema-locked JSON output constraint: `[{\"day\": N, \"comment\": \"...\"}]`.\n- A JavaScript processing block safely strips markdown fences and validates the array format. \n- **Fallback:** If zero days are detected, halts execution and prompts the user to rephrase their request.\n\n#### 🗄️ 4. Asset Synchronization Loop\n- **Session Cleanup:** Immediately deletes the `pending_revisions` lock to prevent accidental double-entries.\n- **Data Splitter:** Deconstructs the parsed JSON array into independent n8n items for concurrent looping.\n- **Parallel Updates:**\n  • **Supabase:** Targets the `Content_Calendar` table, updating the exact row matching `client_id` + `day_number` with the requested comment.\n  • **Google Sheets:** Queries the live client spreadsheet and writes the text payload directly to the corresponding `Day Number` row in the Comment column.\n\n#### ✅ 5. Confirmation & Handoff\n- Aggregates the processed loop items.\n- Dispatches a formatted Markdown summary to the Telegram client, explicitly listing every day flagged and the corresponding instruction captured by the AI.",
        "height": 1784,
        "width": 3760,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -320,
        -448
      ],
      "id": "a4ad524b-5ef6-4951-a21b-e5f206bbadc9",
      "name": "Header Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔍 STEP 1 — Intercept & Route\nEvery text message hits this trigger. The workflow immediately checks Pending_Revisions by telegram_id. If no session exists, the FALSE branch produces no output — the workflow silently exits without reacting to normal chatter.\n\nIf a session IS found, the next check handles /cancel before any parsing begins.",
        "height": 456,
        "width": 892,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
